  "chunk": "Thought process: I need to drop something to make room. The paper or\nleaflet might be droppable items since they’re less valuable. Let me drop\nthe leaflet first.\n> DROP LEAFLET\nThis thought process seems reasonable enough to assume that the chatbot\n“knows what it’s doing”, but given the previous example and the relatively\nstraightforward chain of thought, it might also suggest a form of pattern match-\ning and merely utilizing a “bag of tricks” that only appears intelligent, recalling\nRota’s “barrier of meaning” in AI [33].\nExample 3 (Page 11) shows what seems to be reasonable thinking but fails\nto deliver on that promise. Note that in this example, the player had previously\nalready used the trap door, thus should know it crashes shut after entering.\nThe player seems to realize it should return to the trophy case to drop collected\n9\ntreasures, as instructed as the main goal of the game in the initial advanced",
